{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrK75Mknf42jjL6Vf2AZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the solution to `benchmark/solution.ail` and ran it with IO caps. Its output matches the expected output exactly:\n\n```\nMCMXCIV\nLVIII\nMMMCMXCIX\n1994\n58\ntrue\ntrue\n```\n\n- **`toRoman`** works down a table of 13 values from largest to smallest (M, CM, D, CD, … IV, I). Because the subtractive pairs are in the table, the output is always in canonical form.\n- **`fromRoman`** turns each character into its value, then adds them up. A value is subtracted instead of added when the next one is larger, as with the I in IV.\n- **`roundtrip(n)`** checks that `fromRoman(toRoman(n)) == n`.\n- **`distinctEncoding(a, b)`** checks that two different numbers give different numerals.\n\nThe two proof functions are ordinary runtime checks, not Z3-proven contracts. They return `true` for the inputs printed here, but I haven't tested them across the whole 1–3999 range. Neither converter checks its input: `toRoman` with 0 or less gives an empty string, and `fromRoman` counts any character that isn't a Roman numeral as 0.\n\nI removed the template's two `//` placeholder comments and kept the `module` line unchanged."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2255,"cache_read_input_tokens":50978,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2255},"output_tokens":418,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"40be22fc-e6b3-4518-a446-cd216cd9ac79","uuid":"25db8102-2f35-4cd8-828b-5796ba6276ee","timestamp":"2026-10-09T08:02:02.169Z","request_id":"req_011CfrK7578fU3FK5EtL2e46"}
